      "filename": "M24A1 Chaffee at the 823 Artillery Battle Memorial Park, Taichung, Taiwan. 07-03-2026 (55254718262).jpg",
      "title": "File:M24A1 Chaffee at the 823 Artillery Battle Memorial Park, Taichung, Taiwan. 07-03-2026 (55254718262).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/M24A1_Chaffee_at_the_823_Artillery_Battle_Memorial_Park%2C_Taichung%2C_Taiwan._07-03-2026_%2855254718262%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M24A1_Chaffee_at_the_823_Artillery_Battle_Memorial_Park,_Taichung,_Taiwan._07-03-2026_(55254718262).jpg",
      "width": 4523,
      "height": 3015,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Alan Wilson from Peterborough, Cambs, UK",
      "description": "Designed to replace the M5 Stuart, some 4,731 Chaffee’s were produced between April 1944 and August 1945. Taiwan received 233 Chaffee’s in 1954 under the Sino-US Mutual Defence Treaty and then 56 more in 1966.\nThis is one of several which were upgraded to M24A1 standard, with a Detroit 6V-53T diesel engine and other minor modifications.\n823 Artillery Battle Memorial Park, Taichung, Taiwan.\n\n7th March 2026",
      "dateCreated": "2026-03-07 09:12",
