    {
      "filename": "M108 Self-Propelled Gun at the 823 Artillery Battle Memorial Park, Taichung, Taiwan. 07-03-2026 (55255877419).jpg",
      "title": "File:M108 Self-Propelled Gun at the 823 Artillery Battle Memorial Park, Taichung, Taiwan. 07-03-2026 (55255877419).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8d/M108_Self-Propelled_Gun_at_the_823_Artillery_Battle_Memorial_Park%2C_Taichung%2C_Taiwan._07-03-2026_%2855255877419%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M108_Self-Propelled_Gun_at_the_823_Artillery_Battle_Memorial_Park,_Taichung,_Taiwan._07-03-2026_(55255877419).jpg",
      "width": 4402,
      "height": 2935,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Alan Wilson from Peterborough, Cambs, UK",
      "description": "The M108 was an American, Cold-War era, self-propelled gun, which saw US service between 1962 and 1975. Produced by Cadillac, it had a crew of five and was armed with the M103 105mm howitzer. Taiwan operated one-hundred M108s, forty-five of which were later modernised to T69 standard with an M59 155mm gun. This preserved example is an un-modified M108.\n823 Artillery Battle Memorial Park, Taichung, Taiwan.\n\n7th March 2026",
      "dateCreated": "2026-03-07 09:13",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
